      ":question/problem": "![](images/50/501c3334b225e4f580cc0d245e0cf53a03a7197fe67c0f324c663458a2a75f25.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, $AH^(\u2015)$ bisects $\u2220BAC$.\n\nConsider the following statement:\n\n> *The segments $BH^(\u2015)$ and $CH^(\u2015)$ are congruent.*\n\nThe table below gives the proof of the statement. Select the correct options in the table and thus complete the proof.\n\n|  | Statement | Reason |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | $\u2220AHB\u2245\u2220AHC$ | {{field-1}} |\n| 2 | $AH^(\u2015)\u2245AH^(\u2015)$ | Reflexive property of congruence |\n| 3 | $\u2220BAH\u2245\u2220CAH$ | {{field-2}} |\n| 4 | $\u25b3BAH\u2245\u25b3CAH$ | {{field-3}} |\n| 5 | $BH^(\u2015)\u2245CH^(\u2015)$ | CPCTC |"
